---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { APP, formatPrice, PRICING } from '../../config';
import { ROUTES } from '../../i18n';
---

<PageLayout
  locale="en"
  title="Terms of Use"
  metaTitle="Terms of Use – Ride Streak"
  description="Terms of use for the Ride Streak iPhone app and the Ride Streak Pro subscription."
  paths={ROUTES.terms}
  lastUpdated="6 September 2026"
>
  <h2>1. Scope</h2>
  <p>
    These terms cover use of the Ride Streak iPhone app, offered by {
      APP.developer
    }. Purchases of Ride Streak Pro are made and processed through the Apple
    App Store; Apple's terms apply in addition and take precedence for the
    purchase itself.
  </p>

  <h2>2. What the app does — and does not</h2>
  <p>
    Ride Streak analyses rides that have already been recorded. It reads them
    from Apple Health and, if you enable it, from Strava.
  </p>
  <p>
    Ride Streak <strong>does not record rides</strong>. There is no recording
    feature, no navigation and no route planning. To record you need an Apple
    Watch, a bike computer or another app that writes to Apple Health.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Requirements</h2>
  <p>
    Ride Streak requires an iPhone running iOS {APP.minOs} or later. There is
    no Apple Watch, iPad, Android or web version. Individual features
    additionally require Apple Health permission, a Strava connection or
    RideStreak Cloud.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Free use and Ride Streak Pro</h2>
  <p>
    The app is free to use. Ride Streak Pro is optional and unlocks additional
    features (training load, power analysis, Fitness &amp; Form, 3D Flyover,
    image and video export, calories, iCloud sync).
  </p>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Plan</th><th>Price</th><th>Billing</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>Pro monthly</td>
        <td>{formatPrice(PRICING.monthly, 'en')}</td>
        <td>monthly, renews automatically</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Pro yearly</td>
        <td>{formatPrice(PRICING.yearly, 'en')}</td>
        <td>yearly, renews automatically</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Lifetime</td>
        <td>{formatPrice(PRICING.lifetime, 'en')}</td>
        <td>one-time, does not renew</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    All prices include VAT. The price shown in the App Store at the time of
    purchase is the one that applies; regional differences are possible.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Renewal and cancellation</h2>
  <p>
    Subscriptions renew automatically unless cancelled at least 24 hours before
    the end of the current period. Manage and cancel them in your iPhone
    Settings under your name → Subscriptions. When a subscription ends the app
    remains usable with every free feature. Lifetime is a one-time purchase.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Withdrawal and refunds</h2>
  <p>
    Refunds are handled exclusively by Apple. Request one through
    <a href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com" rel="noopener" target="_blank"
      >reportaproblem.apple.com</a
    >. As a consumer you have the statutory right of withdrawal in relation to
    Apple.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Licence</h2>
  <p>
    You receive a simple, non-transferable right to use Ride Streak on the
    devices associated with your account. Reverse engineering, resale and
    circumventing protection mechanisms are not permitted except where the law
    mandates otherwise.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Warranty and liability</h2>
  <p>
    The values Ride Streak calculates — in particular training load, FTP
    estimate, power zones and wear indicators — are
    <strong>guidance figures</strong>. They replace neither medical advice nor
    a competent inspection of your bicycle. Decisions about training and about
    replacing safety-critical components are yours; when in doubt, have your
    bike checked by a qualified mechanic.
  </p>
  <p>
    We are liable without limitation for intent and gross negligence, for
    injury to life, body or health, and under the German Product Liability Act.
    For ordinary negligence we are liable only for breaches of material
    contractual obligations, limited to the foreseeable damage typical for this
    type of contract.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Third-party trademarks</h2>
  <p>
    Apple, Apple Health, Apple Watch and App Store are trademarks of Apple Inc.
    Strava is a trademark of Strava, Inc.; Garmin and Wahoo are trademarks of
    their respective owners. Ride Streak is not affiliated with, endorsed or
    sponsored by any of them.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Changes and governing law</h2>
  <p>
    We may adapt these terms when the feature set or the legal situation
    changes. German law applies, excluding the UN Convention on Contracts for
    the International Sale of Goods; mandatory consumer protection rules of
    your country of residence remain unaffected.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
